                <pb facs="0311" n="203" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg203"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Mr.
                            Baker.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Gresham directs Mr. Baker to report without delay when the control of the
                    executive power of Nicaragua shall pass with general acquiescence to any
                    government, and to maintain an attitude of impartiality during the deeply
                    deplored continuance of civil dissensions in that country.</p>
            </div>
